Audio Evidence Questions

Produce or analyze a transcript and compare it with a verified transcript.
Identify speakers only as neutral labels unless their identities are independently established.
Extract relevant dates, names, locations, threats, transactions, or statements.
Mark uncertain, inaudible, overlapping, or low-confidence portions.
Separate spoken content from interpretations of tone, intent, or emotion.
Identify background sounds as observations without making unsupported source claims.
Construct a timestamped event list linked to the recording.
Explain how transcription, compression, noise reduction, or other preparation steps affected the result.
